---
import BlogPostLayout from '../../../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro';

const title = "Software Development vs Software Testing: Which Career to Choose in India";
const seoTitle = "Software Development vs Software Testing: Which Career to Choose";
const description = "Software development vs software testing career choice in India: work, skills, entry routes, a decision table, a plan and honest limits.";
const seoDescription = "Choose by the problems you enjoy, then build proof.";
const canonical = "https://futurecareerschool.com/blog/career-options/software-development-vs-software-testing-career-choice-india/";
const publishedDateISO = "2026-10-30";
const publishedDateLabel = "30 October 2026";
const authorName = "Shivanshi Sehgal";
const authorUrl = "https://futurecareerschool.com/about/shivanshi-sehgal/";
const authorRole = "Career researcher and writer";

const faqItems = [
  [
    "Which has better scope?",
    "Both do. Fit with your interests and proof of skill matter more."
  ],
  [
    "Can I move from testing to development?",
    "Often yes, especially through automation."
  ],
  [
    "Is testing easier to enter?",
    "Entry can be easier, but standards still apply. Read notices."
  ],
  [
    "Do testers need to code?",
    "Automation roles do. Manual roles need less."
  ],
  [
    "Which pays more?",
    "It varies by employer and level. Compare notices."
  ],
  [
    "Can I do both?",
    "Yes, in roles that combine them."
  ],
  [
    "Is a degree needed?",
    "Often asked for. Read notices."
  ],
  [
    "Will AI change both?",
    "Routine tasks shrink. Judgment remains."
  ]
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faqItems.map((item) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: item.a },
  })),
};
---

<BlogPostLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  seoTitle={seoTitle}
  seoDescription={seoDescription}
  canonical={canonical}
  category="career-options"
  publishedAt={publishedDateISO}
  publishedLabel={publishedDateLabel}
  authorName={authorName}
  authorUrl={authorUrl}
  authorRole={authorRole}
  jsonLdExtras={[faqJsonLd]}
>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>Software development and software testing both need careful thinking, but developers build features while testers look for how things fail, so the better choice depends on whether you enjoy building or breaking and on how you want to grow.</strong> The decisions that unlock high income opportunities include choosing a branch early and building a high-income skill portfolio of finished work, because AI can handle routine tasks but cannot take responsibility for your results.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Short answer:</strong> Choose by the problems you enjoy, then build proof.</li>
      <li><strong>Evidence:</strong> This page quotes no statistics or pay figures and was not built from fetched sources. Ten live notices and two conversations, as set out below, are the best way to get current local evidence.</li>
      <li><strong>Growth:</strong> Clear proof and finished work support an earlier path to financial freedom.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
    This guide is part of our set of <a href="/blog/career-options/">career option guides</a>. Read it with <a href="/blog/career-guidance/what-career-should-i-choose/">what career should I choose</a>, <a href="/blog/career-guidance/how-to-choose-between-two-career-options-india/">how to choose between two career options</a> and <a href="/blog/skills/how-to-find-which-skills-are-in-demand-in-india/">how to find which skills are in demand</a>.
  </p>

