  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for reliable software and fewer defects. They judge you by samples, careful thinking and how clearly you explain problems.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing a bug report another person can reproduce in one go.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and software development vs software testing: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools generate code and test cases quickly. Routine versions of both shrink.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, product sense and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and check; later, own design and quality decisions.
  </p>

  <h2 id="better">Alternatives that can beat a general software development vs software testing path</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
